Make help page 7 a pad reference card.

Nothing on screen says what the buttons do, and a pad has no labels under the player's
fingers. The help screen already exists and is reachable from the main menu, so the card
is its last page rather than a new screen: the shared controller drawing from
`common/assets/controls` (packaged as `data/gui/oops-controller.png` by this title's
`package` rule, so upstream's `data/` stays as it ships), with the bindings beside it.

The bindings are read from the pad's own configuration when the page opens
(`help_screen_7.cpp`), so the card cannot disagree with the game and follows a rebind.
It is read-only; rebinding stays in Options, Controls.

The page it replaces was "Multiplayer": how to join an online server, and how to set up
several local input devices. The tab is renamed "Controls" on all seven help layouts,
because each one repeats the tab bar.

